---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// About page — the author identity behind Behind the Meter.
//
// Added 2026-08-16. Until now the site published as "Jason", which wasted a real
// credential and blocked two channels: LinkedIn (which needs a real person) and
// Whirlpool (whose rules require declaring a commercial interest).
//
// ⚠️ ACCURACY RULES FOR THIS PAGE — every line here is checkable, so keep it that way:
//   · "since 1998" not "27 years" — a start year never goes stale and never needs editing
//   · The 2024 audits were ENVIRONMENTAL COMPLIANCE audits. Not electrical performance,
//     not yield. Do not let this drift into implying he assessed how much power they made.
//   · No client names. They're on a CV that gets sent to people; that is not the same as
//     a public webpage. Jason's explicit instruction, 2026-08-16.
//   · Self-consumption is 47% — measured, calendar year 2025, ONE house. Never "typical".
//
// Source for the credentials: Jason's own CV, read 2026-08-16.
---
<Layout
  title="About — Behind the Meter | Powermind"
  description="Behind the Meter is written by Jason Watson, an environmental scientist and certified lead environmental auditor in Canberra who measured his own solar for a year."
  active="about">
  <div class="wrap about">

    <h1>About</h1>

    <div class="who">
      {/* Circular PNG with a transparent field — the original headshot has a light grey
          studio background, which would read as a bright rectangle on a near-black page.
          Masking it to a circle removes the box without retouching the photo. */}
      <img class="mug" src="/jason-watson-320.png" width="132" height="132"
           alt="Jason Watson" loading="eager" />
      <div class="who-t">
        <div class="who-n">Jason Watson</div>
        <div class="who-r">Environmental scientist · Certified Lead Environmental Auditor</div>
        <div class="who-l">Canberra, Australia</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lede">
      <p>I've been an environmental scientist since 1998 — measuring things, assessing
         constraints, and working out whether what was promised on paper survives contact
         with a real site.</p>
    </div>

    <p>More recently that's included certification as an <strong>Exemplar Global Lead
       Environmental Auditor</strong>, and in 2024, environmental compliance audits at a
       solar farm in Queensland and a grid-scale battery here in the ACT.</p>

    <p>The job is always some version of the same question: <em>is this actually doing what
       it said it would?</em></p>

    <p>Then I put solar on my own roof, and realised nobody was asking that question about
       my house. So I measured it for a year. <strong>Behind the Meter</strong> is what I
       found, and what I've learned since.</p>

    <h2>What I found, to be going on with</h2>

    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-n">47%</div>
      <div class="stat-t">of what my roof generated in 2025, my house actually used.
        The other 53% went to the grid for a few cents. One Canberra home, measured —
        not an average, and not a claim about yours.</div>
    </div>

    <p>That gap is the whole subject. Not generating more — catching more of what you
       already generate. Most of what I write comes back to it.</p>

    <h2>How I handle numbers</h2>

    <p>Old habit, and it's the useful part of an audit background. Every figure here is
       marked as one of three things:</p>

    <ul class="tags">
      <li><b>Measured</b> — my own house, my own meter. Always described as one home,
        because that's what it is.</li>
      <li><b>Modelled</b> — the calculator's output, with the assumptions visible.</li>
      <li><b>Sourced</b> — someone else's work, cited, and checked that it's current.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>They never get mixed silently. If a number can't be traced to one of those three,
       it doesn't get published — I'd rather leave a gap than fill it convincingly.</p>

    <p>You won't find a guaranteed savings figure anywhere on this site. Nobody can
       promise you one and mean it, because it depends on your tariff, your roof and your
       habits. Ranges with the assumptions showing, or nothing.</p>

    <h2>Why I built Powermind</h2>

    <p>Measuring my own house told me the problem wasn't generating more power. It was
       catching more of what I already generated — running the hot water, the car charger
       and the aircon while the sun was actually on the roof.</p>

    <p>Doing that by hand means paying attention at the right hour, every day, forever.
       Nobody sustains that. So I built software to do it instead.</p>

    <p><a href="/app">Powermind</a> is the science put into practice — the same
       measurements, automated. It's not a separate business that happens to sit next to
       the writing; it's the same work, one step further on.</p>

    <p>Which is also why I'll tell you when something isn't worth buying, including
       something of mine. The sources here are linked and the arithmetic is shown so you
       can check it rather than take my word for it.</p>

    <h2>Credentials</h2>

    <ul class="creds">
      <li>Environmental scientist, practising since 1998</li>
      <li>Exemplar Global Certified Lead Environmental Auditor (ISO 14001)</li>
      <li>Master of Environmental Science, Macquarie University</li>
      <li>Bachelor of Applied Science, University of Canberra</li>
      <li>Founder, <a href="https://futerra.ai" rel="noopener">Futerra</a> — an independent
        Australian software company. Powermind is its first product.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>

    <p>Reply to any edition of the newsletter and it comes straight to me — I read every
       one, and they shape what I write next. Otherwise:
       <a href="mailto:jason@futerra.ai">jason@futerra.ai</a>.</p>

    <p>If you've got solar, a heat pump, an EV or a quote you're weighing up, I'm
       genuinely interested in what your numbers look like.</p>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-teal" href="/behind-the-meter">Read Behind the Meter</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/calculator">Try the calculator</a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .about{max-width:720px;padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:90px}
  .about .eyebrow{color:var(--teal);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px}
  .about h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:800}
  .about .who{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;margin:24px 0 4px}
  .about .mug{width:132px;height:132px;border-radius:50%;flex:0 0 auto;
              box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--line), 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.45)}
  .about .who-n{font-size:22px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink)}
  .about .who-r{margin-top:4px;font-size:14px;color:var(--teal);font-weight:600;line-height:1.45}
  .about .who-l{margin-top:3px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--faint)}
  .about .lede{margin:22px 0 8px;padding:20px 22px;background:var(--bg-1);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
  .about .lede::before{content:'';position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:3px;background:var(--teal)}
  .about .lede p{margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--ink)}
  .about h2{margin:40px 0 12px;font-size:20px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:700}
  .about p{margin-bottom:13px;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--muted)}
  .about p strong{color:var(--ink)}
  .about a{color:var(--amber-lt);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(250,199,117,.35)}
  .about a:hover{border-bottom-color:var(--amber-lt)}
  .about .stat{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start;margin:22px 0 18px;padding:20px 22px;background:var(--bg-1);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px}
  .about .stat-n{font-size:42px;line-height:1;font-weight:800;color:var(--teal);letter-spacing:-.03em;flex:0 0 auto}
  .about .stat-t{font-size:14px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--muted)}
  .about ul.tags,.about ul.creds{margin:0 0 16px;padding:0;list-style:none}
  .about ul.tags li{position:relative;padding-left:18px;margin-bottom:9px;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}
  .about ul.tags li::before{content:'';position:absolute;left:0;top:10px;width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--teal)}
  .about ul.tags b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:650}
  .about ul.creds li{padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:15px;color:var(--muted)}
  .about ul.creds li:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .about .cta-row{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:30px}
  .about .btn-ghost{border:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--ink);background:transparent}
  .about .cta-row a{border-bottom:0}
  @media(max-width:820px){
    .about{padding-top:36px}
    .about h1{font-size:32px}
    .about .stat{flex-direction:column;gap:10px}
    .about .stat-n{font-size:36px}
    .about .who{gap:14px}
    .about .mug{width:96px;height:96px}
    .about .who-n{font-size:19px}
    .about .who-r{font-size:13px}
  }
</style>
